  "evidence_scope": "Identity-ordered pooled titles, resource types and stored descriptions/snippets, with selected ambiguous descriptions inspected. No live source pages, exported rows, PDF contents or actual province/age/sex dimension values were verified. Source URLs identify the recorded evidence only.",
  "limitations": "Single AI assessor, not independent human judgments or adjudication. The assessor also implements the scoring workflow and has prior knowledge of system designs: this is not a blinded independent experiment. OpenSearch uses only 342 downloadable dataflows from the historical baseline; portal searches broader resource types. This pilot neither completes #11/#20 nor selects the production analyzer. Human judges should receive blank sheets without these labels to avoid anchoring.",
  "rubric": {
    "2": "Stored evidence directly supports the target concept and requested population/geography or explicitly advertises a suitable breakdown.",
    "1": "Related context, a narrower/broader measure, revisions, or unconfirmed requested scope; not sufficient as a direct answer.",
    "0": "Unrelated or a different/misleading measure, including enterprise births versus baby births and resident foreigners versus tourists."
  },
