  "query_notes": {
    "q01": "General CPI and its bulletins answer directly; components, weights, selected prices and core measures are context. Producer prices measure a different target.",
    "q02": "Stored labour descriptions explicitly include unemployment rates. Revision histories are contextual; demographic dependency and emissions are different indicators.",
    "q03": "GDP bulletins directly cover the target. PPP/per-capita comparisons provide context rather than aggregate domestic GDP. Other domestic/foreign word matches are unrelated.",
    "q04": "ADNKS population outputs and system metadata are direct discovery targets. Foreign-only population, density, median age and name rankings are narrower context.",
    "q05": "Housing sales totals and bulletins answer directly; buyer-sex shares and foreign-buyer subsets are context. Generic trade, employment and waste statistics do not answer.",
    "q06": "Industrial production indices and bulletins are direct; revisions and contributions are context. Construction/services production measure different sectors.",
    "q07": "TÜFE means consumer prices. Apply the same intent and grades as q01; similarly spelled unrelated words and service trade are not matches.",
    "q08": "Unqualified ÜFE is interpreted broadly as producer prices, including service, agriculture, domestic and external indices. Item prices and weights are contextual; consumer prices are a different indicator.",
    "q09": "Yİ-ÜFE specifically requests domestic producer prices. Combined domestic/external totals and domestic contributions are context. Agricultural or external-only series do not answer that target.",
    "q10": "GSYH has the same GDP intent as q03. Per-capita PPP comparisons remain contextual.",
    "q11": "HİA means Household Labour Force Survey. Metadata explicitly names HİA; labour tables provide partial context. Marital-status population tables use ADNKS, not HİA.",
    "q12": "ADNKS abbreviation has the same system/population intent as q04. Foreign-only population, median age and name rankings are narrower context.",
    "q13": "Inflation is interpreted as consumer-price inflation; producer prices, weights and selected prices offer related context.",
    "q14": "Cost of living maps primarily to consumer prices. Life-satisfaction descriptions explicitly mention cost-of-living concerns, so they provide context; survival/life tables and name rankings do not.",
    "q15": "National income maps to aggregate GDP, with PPP GDP contextual. Company income statements, public receipts, investment returns and incubators do not measure national income.",
    "q16": "People unable to find work map to unemployed/jobseeker statistics. Recruitment difficulty is the employer perspective; software adoption and already-employed distributions are different targets.",
    "q17": "Birth-event bulletins answer counts. Birth rates and birth-order proportions are related but not counts. Population by birthplace and enterprise births/deaths must not be mistaken for babies born.",
    "q18": "Dış satım means exports. Trade bulletins answer directly; terms of trade, export-related prices and trade indices provide partial context.",
    "q19": "Inflected unemployment retains the q02 intent. Youth-only tables and revisions are narrower context; provincial unemployment is an available direct geographic breakdown.",
    "q20": "Population counts/distributions answer the broad intent. Density, household size and specialized population subgroups are contextual. Nonparticipation reasons and NEET-only tables do not answer general population.",
    "q21": "Require an explicit province population breakdown or an Istanbul population snippet for full relevance. Generic geography dimensions do not establish Istanbul coverage; national population/density tables remain context.",
    "q22": "Unqualified price changes can be consumer or producer prices. Selected price levels are contextual. Wage, employment, hours and agricultural output changes are different quantities.",
    "q23": "Broad export intent: general export value/volume indices and trade bulletins directly relate. Exclusion-specific indices and enterprise-cohort economic indicators are narrower context.",
    "q24": "Inflected housing-sales intent matches q05. Adjusted housing sales are direct; buyer nationality/sex subsets are contextual; web and retail-trade sales are different targets.",
    "q25": "ASCII unemployment-rate query has the q02 intent. Literacy, emissions, dependency, brain-drain, web sales and price rates are different indicators.",
    "q26": "ASCII population query retains the broad population intent. Foreign-only population, municipality-only population, density/growth and literacy are partial context.",
    "q27": "ASCII consumer-price query has the same intent as q01, including the distinction between the aggregate index and weights/components/prices.",
    "q28": "Youth unemployment requires the youth group: basic-indicator descriptions explicitly include ages 15–24. NEET and all-age unemployment are context, not equivalent youth-unemployment measures.",
    "q29": "ASCII Istanbul population has the same geographic requirement as q21. National totals or generic geographic field names cannot establish province coverage.",
    "q30": "ASCII foreign trade covers general import/export and international services. Exclusion-specific indices are partial context. Domestic retail/service-confidence series and birthplace are different concepts.",
    "q31": "Typo is interpreted as enflasyon. CPI metadata directly answers; national statistical compendia are broader context. Inflation-adjusted company accounts do not measure inflation itself.",
    "q32": "Typo is interpreted as unemployment; match the labour targets and revision treatment in q02. Construction cost is a different measure.",
    "q33": "Population typo has exactly the q26 information need and corresponding metadata-based judgments.",
    "q34": "Housing-sales typo retains q05 intent. Household size/structure is not a transaction count; foreign-buyer housing subsets are context.",
    "q35": "Consumer-price typo is interpreted as CPI; spatial price levels and basket/selected prices provide context. Corporate accounts and agricultural producer prices do not measure consumer prices.",
    "q36": "Industrial-production typo targets industry indices/bulletins. Manufacturing structure, environmental production and revision/contribution measures are context; construction/services/crops are different sectors.",
    "q37": "Full relevance requires joint youth AND female unemployment coverage. Basic-indicator metadata advertises ages 15–24 and sex; separate female participation and total-youth unemployment snippets do not establish the joint rate.",
    "q38": "Seasonally adjusted unemployment targets basic/complementary labour indicators. Adjusted employment is context; adjusted CPI, exports, sales and construction are different measures.",
    "q39": "Require age-specific population counts. Foreign-born-only population, ratios and general ADNKS metadata/bulletins are partial context unless an explicit age-count table is identified. Child internet usage is not population counts.",
    "q40": "Sectoral export quantity requires both sector and quantity. Export indices advertise sector fields but do not verify absolute quantities; value/volume bulletins and price indices are partial context. Import quantities are a different direction.",
    "q41": "First-hand housing counts appear explicitly in bulletin snippets; sales-status tables can provide that breakdown. Other housing subsets and adjusted total sales are context.",
    "q42": "Annual consumer-price change is explicit in CPI bulletin snippets and general CPI tables. Category changes, weights and selected prices are narrower context; producer prices and consumer sentiment are different indicators.",
    "q43": "All candidates concern exports but stored metadata does not establish Ankara coverage. No candidate gets full relevance merely from a generic geography dimension.",
    "q44": "Istanbul population shares q21/q29 geographic criteria: explicit province-count tables and the 2025 Istanbul snippet are direct; national or restricted population measures are context.",
    "q45": "Province-level sales-status counts can answer Izmir housing sales. National totals and narrower foreign-buyer subsets are context; stored bulletin snippets do not establish Izmir coverage.",
    "q46": "Industry-related candidates offer national/sectoral context, but none of the stored descriptions establishes Bursa-specific industry coverage. No full-relevance provincial result is asserted.",
    "q47": "Tourism bulletins offer national tourism context without confirmed Antalya coverage. Resident foreigners are not visitors; producer agricultural prices are unrelated.",
    "q48": "Provincial birth rates directly address a broad province/birth query. National birth bulletins and birth-order proportions are context. Birthplace population stocks, names and enterprise births are different concepts."
  },
